{"format_version":1,"partition":25469,"records":{"-bar":{"entries":[["-bar",null,"/baːɐ̯/","From Middle High German -bære, from Old High German -bāri, from Proto-Germanic *bēriz.\nThe modern vowel -a- is after the adverb form (Middle High German -bāre, Old High German -bāro), which came to be used in predicative and then also in attributive position. This development was especially Low and Central German (compare Middle Low German -bār(e) alongside -bēr(e)). Also cognate with Dutch -baar, West Frisian -ber, Alemannic German -bar, Old English -bǣre. Old Norse -bærr (Old Swedish -bǣr). This suffix is said to be West Germanic, so the Old Norse form is probably an early Middle Low German borrowing."]],"senses":[[52687,"-bar","suffix","-able, -ible",0]]},"abderitischem":{"entries":[["abderitischem",null,null,null]],"senses":[[442687,"abderitischem","adj","strong dative masculine/neuter singular of abderitisch",0]],"inflections":[["abderitischem","abderitisch","dative,masculine,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"böseren":{"entries":[["böseren",null,null,null]],"senses":[[149565,"böseren","adj","inflection of böse:",0],[149566,"böseren","adj","strong genitive masculine/neuter singular comparative degree",1],[149567,"böseren","adj","weak/mixed genitive/dative all-gender singular comparative degree",2],[149568,"böseren","adj","strong/weak/mixed accusative masculine singular comparative degree",3],[149569,"böseren","adj","strong dative plural comparative degree",4],[149570,"böseren","adj","weak/mixed all-case plural comparative degree",5]],"inflections":[["böseren","böse","comparative,genitive,masculine,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"durchvögelte":{"entries":[["durchvögelte",null,null,null]],"senses":[[666314,"durchvögelte","verb","inflection of durchvögeln:",0],[666315,"durchvögelte","verb","first/third-person singular dependent preterite",1],[666316,"durchvögelte","verb","first/third-person singular dependent subjunctive II",2]],"inflections":[["durchvögelte","durch